/; EXPECT_ERROR: FunctionNotFound
/; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
/; REGRESSION: a misspelled name under `spawn` used to report only "'spawn'
/; expects a function call", hiding the real problem.
/;
/; When binding the call fails on its own terms the binder already reported a
/; precise message with a useful location. Adding the generic spawn error on
/; top buried it, so the failure is now propagated silently.
/; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

spawn thisFunctionDoesNotExist()
